# Demolition Field: "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice this land: Destroy target nonbasic land an opponent controls." Bot2's basic Island and
# Bot1's own nonbasic Tundra are refused as targets, Bot2's Bazaar of Baghdad is destroyed. Then, in the order of the text,
# "that land's controller" (Bot2) may search for a basic land (Forest) and "you" (Bot1) may search for one (Plains - the
# nonbasic Tundra in the library is not a basic land card, CR 205.4a). Both lands enter untapped.

[Bot1 Deck]
Tundra
Island
Demolition Field
Island x14
Tundra
Island
Plains

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Bazaar of Baghdad
Island x16
Island
Island
Forest

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Tundra.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Bazaar of Baghdad.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Demolition Field.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Tundra.Activate(Ability: {W})
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
! Bot1.Battlefield.Demolition Field.Activate(Ability: Destroy; Bot2.Battlefield.Island)
! Bot1.Battlefield.Demolition Field.Activate(Ability: Destroy; Bot1.Battlefield.Tundra)
Bot1.Battlefield.Demolition Field.Activate(Ability: Destroy; Bot2.Battlefield.Bazaar of Baghdad)
Bot2.Accept
Bot2.Search(Forest)
Bot1.Accept
! Bot1.Search(Tundra)
Bot1.Search(Plains)

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Demolition Field
Bot1.Battlefield = Tundra; Island; Plains
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Tapped = false
Bot2.Graveyard = Bazaar of Baghdad
Bot2.Battlefield = Island; Forest
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Tapped = false
